## What happened

In .NET 11, **DSA (Digital Signature Algorithm) was removed from macOS**. Calling `DSA.Create()` now throws on macOS. Windows and Linux are unaffected.

## How to fix

Since you're *verifying legacy signatures* (not creating new ones), you have two options:

**Option A — Platform-guard DSA to non-macOS only:**

```csharp
if (OperatingSystem.IsMacOS())
    throw new PlatformNotSupportedException("DSA verification not supported on macOS in .NET 11+");
```

**Option B (recommended) — Migrate to ECDSA or RSA:**

```csharp
// Replace DSA.Create() with a modern algorithm
using var ecdsa = ECDsa.Create();
bool valid = ecdsa.VerifyData(data, signature, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);
```

If you must continue verifying existing DSA signatures cross-platform, you'll need a software-only DSA implementation (e.g., via BouncyCastle) for macOS, since the platform no longer provides one. On Windows/Linux, `DSA.Create()` still works (though DSA is considered legacy everywhere).
